        "description": "- Coverage SLO (critical), per collection tier\n  polled/targeted dropped below 0.95 for one tier - significant silent loss in that tier.\n  Grouped `by (tier)` instead of one cross-tier ratio: after the tier split all four snmp CronJobs sweep the same fleet and each publishes its own polled/targeted pair, so a summed ratio stays ~1.0 even while one tier collapses entirely - the failure is averaged away. `by (tier)` is also the safe idiom across the split itself: until the tiered jobs deploy no series carries a `tier` label at all, every series groups into a single unlabelled instance, and this rule reads exactly as the untiered rule did. Never write `{tier=\"critical\"}` here - see the tier-label trap in ALERTS_NOTES.md.\n  Action: investigate the collection pipeline for the tier named on the alert immediately.",
